1368:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 				   \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC0_CH0, @ref XMC_USIC0_CH1 to @ref XMC_USIC2_CH1 based on device su
1369:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * @param  event Transmit FIFO events to be cleared. \n
1370:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 			     \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC_CH_TXFIFO_EVENT_STANDARD, @ref XMC_USIC_CH_TXFIFO_EVENT_ERROR.
1371:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * @return None
1372:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
1373:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Description</b><br>
1374:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Clears the transmit FIFO event flags in the status register. \n\n
1375:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * USIC channel peripheral does not clear the event flags after they are read.
1376:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * This API clears the events provided in the \a mask value. 
1377:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * XMC_USIC_CH_TXFIFO_EVENT enumeration can be used as input. Multiple events
1378:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * can be cleared by providing a mask value obtained by bitwise OR operation of 
1379:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * multiple event enumerations.
1380:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
1381:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
